Purpose

This folder contains evaluation standards for the Trackflow logistics website. It helps the AI agent verify that the website is accessible, responsive, functional, secure, and maintainable.

Website Scope

Trackflow provides e-commerce logistics services in the United States and Spain, including:

Warehouse management

Last-mile delivery

Returns management

Customized logistics proposals through a contact form

Evaluation Categories

Accessibility: Semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, labels, contrast, and screen-reader support.

Responsiveness: Layout behavior on mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop screens.

Form Validation: Required fields, valid email addresses, helpful error messages, and safe submission handling.

Code Quality: HTML structure, CSS organization, JavaScript reliability, maintainability, and security.

How the Agent Should Evaluate

Read the website source code before making changes.

Identify the relevant pages, forms, fields, styles, and JavaScript handlers.

Execute the test cases in test-cases.md.

Review every applicable item in website-checklist.md.

Record each result as PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED, or NOT APPLICABLE.

Include evidence for failures, such as the affected file, line number when available, and steps to reproduce.

Fix issues only when authorized, then rerun the affected tests.

Never report a test as passed unless it has actually been verified.

Evaluation Status Definitions

PASS: The expected behavior has been verified.

FAIL: The website does not meet the requirement.

BLOCKED: The test cannot be completed because a dependency or environment is unavailable.

NOT APPLICABLE: The requirement does not apply to the implementation.

Completion Criteria

The website is ready for review when all applicable critical tests pass, no unresolved critical accessibility or security issues remain, and any known limitations are documented.

A contact form must not be considered production-ready merely because it displays a success message. Verify that the submission reaches a real, authorized backend or form service and that errors are handled correctly.